course: dictionary
lesson: 3077
title: Edit: checking and improving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To edit writing is to check it and change it to make it better. You fix mistakes and choose stronger words. «Editing means improving the writing, like a stronger word or a clearer order.»
explain: Editing is not the same as proofreading. Proofreading hunts the small slips, such as spelling, punctuation, and a tense that wanders from «went» to «go». Editing looks at the bigger picture too: is the order clear, and is anything missing?
explain: Edit has other meanings. People edit photos and videos by cutting and arranging them, and an edit is one change made in this way. To check your meaning, swap in a word like improve or change and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Edit (verb) means to check writing and change it to make it better.
fact: To edit a film, photo or video is to cut and arrange it.
fact: «Edit out» means remove something, so it is no longer there.
fact: Editing looks at the bigger things, like word choice and order; proofreading checks the small slips, like spelling.
fact: «Many online photos are filtered or edited», so the picture is not always the real person.
exercise: «Editing means improving the writing, like a stronger word or a clearer order.» What does edit mean here? | To read it out loud | *To check and change writing to make it better | To delete the whole page | To write a brand new story from nothing
exercise: «Many online photos are filtered or edited.» What does edited mean in this sentence? | Taken by a camera with no flash | *Changed by cutting or adjusting the picture | Printed on paper | Shared with lots of friends
exercise: Which job hunts the small slips, such as spelling and punctuation? | Publishing a book | *Proofreading | Choosing a photo frame | Planning a story
test: Ella's teacher says, «Edit your work before you publish it.» What should Ella do? | Leave it as it is because it is already finished | Put it on a shelf and forget about it | *Check it and improve it by fixing mistakes and choosing better words
test: «The editor cut the scene and then decided to edit out the boring part.» What does edit out mean? | *Remove the boring part | Print the boring part twice | Add a picture of the boring part | Shout the boring part loudly
exam: A friend says, «Editing is just the same as checking spelling.» Which answer is best? | Yes, they mean exactly the same thing | *No, editing also improves word choice and order, while proofreading checks spelling | No, editing means painting pictures | Yes, and you never need to check spelling again
